 *   **Precision:** Distance calculations and frustum tests should use sufficient precision to avoid jittering or incorrect culling, especially near threshold boundaries [G].
-*   **Boundary Conditions:** The distance thresholds (`_world_size / 2`, `_world_size / 4`) are strict inequalities in the source. Care must be taken to handle points exactly on these boundaries consistently [S1, unofficial].
 
